lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1021</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1375</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ec.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">989</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Phd.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">60e</span> </span>: freq. in Platonic dialogue, <span class=\"gk\">πῶς λέγεις</span>; how <b class=\"lex-tr\">do you mean</b>? in what <b class=\"lex-tr\">sense do you say this? Ap.</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24e</span> </span>, al.; <span class=\"gk\">ἢ πῶς λέγομεν</span>; or what <b class=\"lex-tr\">do we mean to say? Grg.</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">480b</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">πῶς δὴ οὖν αὐτὸ λέγεις</span>; <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Phdr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">265c</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ποῖόν τί ποτε ἄρα λέγοντ ές φασι</span>.. what they can possibly <b class=\"lex-tr\">mean</b> by saying.., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Tht.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">181c</span> </span>, al.: c. dupl. acc., <span class=\"gk\">τοιοῦτόν τι σὲ λέγειν τὸ κρεῖττον</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Grg.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">489d</span> </span>, al.: freq. (esp. in Trag.) to explain more fully, <span class=\"gk\">εἴσω κομίζου καὶ σύ, Κασάνδραν λέγω</span> you, <b class=\"lex-tr\">I mean</b> Cassandra, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1035</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ὁ μάντις, υἱὸν Οἰκλέους λ.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">609</span> </span